Subject: Smart quotes that arent latin-1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=iso-8859-1
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The header says iso-8859-1, but the body is really windows-1252: the
bytes below fall in the C1 control range that latin-1 leaves undefined.

“Curly quotes”, an em dash — like this, an ellipsis…, a bullet • and a
trademark™. Strict latin-1 decoding turns these into control characters;
every real client silently treats iso-8859-1 as windows-1252 instead.
